WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
31 January 2020, 11 pm.

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:07.230
The UK leaves the European Union.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:14.130
In 2025, the UK exported 913.2
billion pounds of goods and services.

4
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:19.730
And the EU, as a group, still
took 40.7 per cent of them.

5
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:25.710
That year, UK ports handled
428.3 million tonnes of freight.

6
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.410
So why is the EU still
its biggest customer?

7
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.590
Just habit?

8
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.730
In this mission, you'll map
the UK's links with the world,

9
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.990
from trade to culture.

10
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.370
Then you'll compare its ties with
the EU and with the Commonwealth.

11
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:46.450
Your mission: explain why the UK still
sells more to the EU than anywhere else.
